                        "entry_id": "3e79bddc-b893-31bb-8a50-d0aef22fb6f6",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Ilex paraguariensis, a species of holly native to southern South America; or the dried leaves and twigs of this plant, used to make the caffeine-rich beverage maté."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "uncountable",
                            "usually"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "25efe2fd-af93-42e9-b26f-e1cf7ecc8ecc",
                                "sense_id": "44d16b90-6edb-3dd3-927d-5e4df62c152f",
                                "text": "The storehouses at Talcahuano had been burst open, and great bags of cotton, yerba, and other valuable merchandise were scattered on the shore."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "56ea7c05-6d88-4c45-8353-550d0af89429",
                                "sense_id": "44d16b90-6edb-3dd3-927d-5e4df62c152f",
                                "text": "This was the place at which the leaves and small sprigs of the yerba tree, when brought from the woods, were first scorched--fire being set to the logs of wood within it."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "2dc0037b-47c8-488f-b5f3-a00abe4d9429",
                                "sense_id": "44d16b90-6edb-3dd3-927d-5e4df62c152f",
                                "text": "His preparations for breakfast are simple, and he is ready to start out after half an hour spent in imbibing a few mates full of yerba infusion."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
